# Text is LF in the working tree on every platform. Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true) otherwise
# turns it into CRLF, which breaks things quietly: a shell script with CRs ("bash\r: No such file"),
# and files of boot-arguments (devices/*/soc.args) whose lines are joined into the kernel's command
# line with a CR left inside every value. Git tells text from binary by content, so nothing here has
# to list the binaries.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A patch is not converted at all: the Mu-Silicium files it patches have CRLF line endings upstream, and
# the context lines of its hunks carry them (BootManager.c, BootManagerLib.inf). Turning them into LF
# would make the patch fail to apply.
*.patch -text

# Unified diff context intentionally starts with a space.
ios26/bootstrap.patch -whitespace
